  "summary": "Architectural tradition of the Sepik River region featuring ceremonial spirit houses adorned with elaborate carvings and paintings that embody ancestral spirits.",
  "description": "Haus tambaran structures are characterized by towering rooflines, massive posts carved with anthropomorphic and zoomorphic figures, and painted gable boards depicting creation stories and supernatural beings. These buildings serve as ritual centers where men gather for ceremonies, initiations, and community decisions, with architectural elements that reflect the spiritual cosmology of Sepik cultures.",
